  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "imperative: polite requests (Can I have ...?)",
      "title_form": "Peticiones corteses: Can I have ...?",
      "title_target": "Polite Requests: Can I have ...?",
      "description_md_form": "Para pedir algo de forma **cortés** en un restaurante o café, usamos **Can I have ...?** (¿Puedo tener...?). Es la forma más común y educada de ordenar.\n\n**Estructura:**\n\n**Can I have** + comida o bebida + **, please?**\n\nEjemplos:\n- **Can I have** a coffee, please?\n- **Can I have** the menu, please?\n\nTambién puedes usar **Can I ...?** con otros verbos:\n- **Can I order** the fish?\n- **Can I pay** the bill?\n\nEsta estructura es más cortés que el imperativo directo (*Give me...*). En inglés, **siempre** preguntamos antes de pedir.",
      "description_md_target": "To ask for something **politely** in a restaurant or café, we use **Can I have ...?**. It is the most common and polite way to order.\n\n**Structure:**\n\n**Can I have** + food or drink + **, please?**\n\nExamples:\n- **Can I have** a coffee, please?\n- **Can I have** the menu, please?\n\nYou can also use **Can I ...?** with other verbs:\n- **Can I order** the fish?\n- **Can I pay** the bill?\n\nThis structure is more polite than the direct imperative (*Give me...*). In English, we **always** ask before ordering.",
      "grammar_structure": "Can I have + [food/drink] + , please?",
      "conjugation_table": null,
      "examples": [
        {
          "id": "exm_gex_001",
          "lexeme_id": null,
          "chunk_id": null,
          "grammar_slug": "imperative: polite requests (Can I have ...?)",
